   ◇ Ada reflects: She thinks him ungrateful, because he has gone away and left her to pay the whole rent herself.
   ◇ Ada reflects: She thinks him a humbug, because he pretended to be sorry for her, and charged her an extra shilling for the trouble.
   ◇ Arthur reflects: He thinks Mr. Thomas a thoroughly honest, upright man, because he has never found a single error in the quarterly ledger, which has passed under his examination.
   ◇ Mr. Thomas reflects: He thinks her sensible, because she is punctual.
   ◇ Mr. Thomas reflects: He thinks him honest, because he is punctual and methodical.

--- Mrs. Ada Turner's diary, Sunday, the 4th of January, 1931 (3/5 key facts kept) ---
To-day I pawned my husband's silver watch for 10s., and my wedding ring for 5s.

--- Mr. Arthur Hale's diary, Sunday, the 4th of January, 1931 (5/5 key facts kept) ---
To-day I balanced the quarterly ledger, and Mr. Thomas expressed himself satisfied with the result.

--- Mr. Walter Thomas's diary, Sunday, the 4th of January, 1931 (2/2 key facts kept) ---
To-day I finished balancing the quarterly ledger, and found £39 18s. 7d. in hand.
   ☾ Ada (forgotten by morning): She dreamt that she went to the coal office and asked for a sack of coals, and the clerk said, "No trust."
   ☾ Arthur (forgotten by morning): He dreamt that he was reading in a great library full of books, and that all at once the walls of the room expanded, and he found himself in a vast plain covered with books, which stretched away, and away, and away, into the distance.
   ☾ Mr. Thomas: He dreamt that he was reading Trollope in an armchair by the fireside, and listening to the wireless talks on Sunday ni, when suddenly an old friend walked in.

