--- Mrs. Ada Turner's diary, Monday, the 5th of January, 1931 (0/2 key facts kept) ---
I was sorry to hear of the death of Princess Louise, the King's eldest sister.

--- Mr. Arthur Hale's diary, Monday, the 5th of January, 1931 (0/1 key facts kept) ---
I read in the Daily Herald that Princess Louise was showing increased weakness; also that Millwall beat Charlton by six goals to nil.

--- Mr. Walter Thomas's diary, Monday, the 5th of January, 1931 (0/0 key facts kept) ---
I read in The Times the announcement of the death of Princess Louise, the King's eldest sister, and, although she has been seriously ill for some months, the recurrence of her heart trouble was indicated by an official bulletin early to-day.
