--- Mr. Arthur Hale's diary, Thursday, the 8th of January, 1931 (3/3 key facts kept) ---
I received a letter from Mr. Walter Thomas; I wrongly entered a figure in the audit books; I resolved never again to make an entry in the books, unless I was perfectly sure that it was correct; I wrote to Mr. Thomas; and I correctly entered the total in the audit books, which are 5778.

--- Mr. Walter Thomas's diary, Thursday, the 8th of January, 1931 (1/1 key facts kept) ---
1. Told Mr. Hale that the auditors come on Monday.
   ☾ Ada (forgotten by morning): She dreamt that she saw Lizzie standing at a street corner in London, and Lizzie said something was wrong with Bert.
   ☾ Arthur: He dreamt that he was being rated by Mr. Thomas for not having the books ready for the auditors.
   ☾ Mr. Thomas (forgotten by morning): He dreamt that he and Hale walked together in the fields, and Hale told him that he aspired to be chief clerk, but feared he should never have courage to speak to Mr. Thomas about it.

